  evidence:
  - evidence_type: LLM_SUGGESTION
    source: https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3101863/
    notes: TOGO M2852 and Bernarde2010 Methods, Bacterial Growth Conditions, identify
      Wilkins-Chalgren agar (Oxoid) used as plates supplemented with10% human blood
      and antibiotics. The article does not establish pre-poured procurement, supplier
      preparation of basal plates, or the sequence of supplementation and plate formation.
      This owner denotes the named Oxoid agar material used in that context; its physical
      purchase form and catalog are unknown. Current CM0619 powder is a comparator,
      not proof of the study procurement. Blood and antibiotics are separate receiving-medium
      additions; no dry-product formula is borrowed.
